# Q18 — how Forge identifies a stack ABILITY (its id is the permanent still on
# the battlefield) versus a stack SPELL (whose card is not). Seat 0 (human)
# controls Shivan Dragon: a permanent with exactly one REPEATABLE, non-tap,
# no-target activated ability that uses the stack ({R}: +1/+0), not
# summoning sick, plus three untapped Mountains — enough mana to activate it
# more than once in the same window, so Forge still offers the permanent
# again while its own ability sits on the stack (the precondition Q18's e2e
# needs: the bug only shows when the source is selectable AT THE SAME TIME
# as its ability is on the stack — a once-only TAP ability like Prodigal
# Sorcerer's "tap: deal 1 damage" taps itself away the instant it is
# activated, so the source is never offered again while its ability sits on
# the stack and the bug's precondition can never occur — see
# docs/planning/wave33-evidence/q18-mutation.md). Seat 1 (ai) has nothing.
